# Keep local secrets and dev state out of the worker image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file the documented
# `docker build -t kyc-sentinel .` baked the local .env — DATABASE_URL today,
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_JUDGE / GROQ_API_KEY once "Running
# live" is wired — into an image layer, where it survives in the pushed
# Artifact Registry image and in `docker history`. The CI path was only
# incidentally safe because gcloud synthesises a .gcloudignore from
# .gitignore; the local build had nothing protecting it.

# Secrets and local runtime state
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.agent-history.log
.agent-rfc/fixtures/sync_state.json
.agent-rfc/fixtures/token_velocity_cache.json
.agent-rfc/fixtures/eval_results.json
.agent-rfc/fixtures/knowledge_graph.json

# VCS and CI — not needed at runtime, and .git carries the full history
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Python build/test artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

# Docs — the worker doesn't read them
DEVLOG.md
README.md
